WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.573
- [Joanna] The time has
come for 3G to pass on.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.920
- 3G network, which means
you can surf the web.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.140
- [Narrator] Some people
will like finding their way

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.350
twice as fast.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.766
- Can you hear me now?

00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:12.240
Good.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.870
- [Joanna] But before,
I had to say goodbye

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.960
by testing 3G one last time.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.461
I'm calling you on my iPhone 3G on 3G.

00:00:21.461 --> 00:00:23.230
(caller laughs)

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.770
- Why did I do this?

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.830
Because, well, I love old tech,

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.610
but also because this year,

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.700
the three big U.S. cellular
carriers are sunsetting

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.530
their once groundbreaking 3G networks.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.590
AT&amp;T will be the first
hitting the 3G kill switch

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.650
on February 22nd.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.750
The rest will be dead by December.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.770
They're all doing this to free up spectrum

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.920
for their 5G networks.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.480
Even now you can't activate
a 3G phone on those networks.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.580
Something I learned the hard way,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.370
trying to get these two phones to work

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.890
in the last couple of weeks.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.980
This iPhone 3G, I got it
handling calls and texts

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.820
on H2O wireless.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.210
And then this iPhone 4,
I finally got working

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.110
on Cricket Wireless for data,

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.637
but 3G service would get cut
off every few hours or so.

00:01:08.637 --> 00:01:10.620
- [Electronic Voice] Thank you
for calling cricket wireless.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.490
- [Operator] And you're
saying you want you to

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.440
reactivate your line?

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.273
- Yes.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:16.960
Both cricket and H2O wireless
use the AT&amp;T network.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.360
But the end of 3G is not just the end

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.420
of some network technology.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.260
This is a moment to remember
that 3G really gave birth

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.960
to the modern day smartphone.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.040
So I tried to go back in time,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.830
challenging myself to
use these old iPhones

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.463
on this old network.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.220
Mission one, use the
web to find a charger.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.040
So yeah, this iPhone
4 is constantly dying.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.160
Phone died again.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.360
Phone shut down again.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.420
Phone's dead again.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.810
Phone shut down again.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.290
It works pretty well when it's plugged in.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.253
So I went on a search for a new,

00:01:52.157 --> 00:01:53.597
charger best buy.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.790
I missed that loading of the blue bar.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:57.710
I won't make you wait.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.952
It took the iPhone 4 on 3G,

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:02.320
39 seconds to load the site.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.060
It took the iPhone 12 Pro on
4G, less than five seconds.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.770
Sure, that's insanely slow.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.610
And right now these images don't load well

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.620
because the browser is so
outdated and mobile versions

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.580
of websites today require more bandwidth.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.740
But you have to remember that before 3G,

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.370
we had 2G or Edge, which was fine

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.850
for quickly getting texts and email,

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.960
but horrible for loading
webpages or any other images.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.623
- We're off to the races here.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:33.010
3G 2.8 times faster.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.263
- [Joanna] Mission to get an Uber.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.760
So this is sort of amazing.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.190
This iPhone 4 running iOS
5.1 from back in 2010,

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.090
had the Uber app installed.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.770
I tried logging in with
my username and password,

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.990
but first I got a lot of this.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:52.070
And then it says my Uber
account has been disabled.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.440
Of course, that has nothing to do with 3G.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.480
This version of the Uber app
is old and it's not supported

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.750
anymore by the company.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:02:59.780
Just gonna wait.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.310
So I had to use my 5G
iPhone 12 to get an Uber.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:06.100
It's a bummer because
3G was actually crucial

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.920
to getting new apps like Uber started.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.110
So I called up someone
who had an insider view

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:14.350
when the app revolution
was just getting started.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.312
Hi Ralph.

00:03:15.312 --> 00:03:16.610
- [Ralph] Yes.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.290
- Hey, it's Joanna from
the Wall Street Journal.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.550
How are you?

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.060
- [Ralph] Hey, fine Joanna, how are you?

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.510
- That's Ralph de la Vega.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.000
He was the CEO of AT&amp;T mobility

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.200
when the first iPhones were introduced

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.550
and were exclusive to AT&amp;T.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.161
- [Ralph] We met with the
Uber team and they asked us

00:03:32.161 --> 00:03:35.747
to help them finance the iPhones
that were going to be given

00:03:35.747 --> 00:03:37.120
to the drivers.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.300
They explained to us what
they were planning to do

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.900
with smartphones, with
mobile broadband technology,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:47.090
and with this amazing,
easy-to-use interface

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:50.020
that use the GPS capability on the iPhone.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.610
And it was an aha! moment.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.943
- Mission three, post a photo.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.183
So yes, I finally made it to Best Buy.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.750
Success.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.360
Of course, I had to brag about it

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.973
by posting on social media,

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.943
which was also fueled by
the mobile revolution.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.240
Except yet again,

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.220
the Instagram app was too old
and the website didn't load.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.000
I got luckier with Facebook.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.570
The upload failed a few times,

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.340
why upload failed,

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.330
but then I was finally
able to get it to work

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.290
via the mobile Facebook site.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:27.810
But remember this photo was
small, just 160 kilobytes.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.550
A selfie taken with the
iPhone 12 is much bigger.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.203
Look, everyone, 3G,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.350
3G, woo hoo!

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.900
3G, before it dies.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.690
And this video wasn't
even HD let alone 4k.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.870
As smartphone cameras got
better, we also got 4G,

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:48.610
which was even faster for all
the things photo and video.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.010
It also brought even
better video streaming.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:52.310
And it's why around that time,

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.660
we started to see bigger
displays on our phones.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.660
And that brings us full
circle, with 3G going away,

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.760
making more room for 5G.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:03.860
3G unlocked these new apps
and gave us an inkling

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.490
of what we could do on our new

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.580
go anywhere, pocket computers.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.420
They also made us realize
that we needed speed

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.330
and 4G made it all faster
to do everything else

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.893
we do on our modern big screen phones.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.410
5G is well, 5G is supposed
to do something better

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.740
than all that.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:25.263
- [Ralph] This technology
with faster download speeds,

00:05:26.453 --> 00:05:30.440
less latency and accuracy
to pinpoint location

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.700
even better than the prior technologies,

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.960
tells me that we're going to see

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.380
another cycle of incredible innovation.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:41.333
- So thank you 3G, rest in peace.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:45.610
I will kinda miss you.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.593
Probably not.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.873
Can I borrow your 5G phone?

00:05:51.329 --> 00:05:52.870
- [Kenny] Sure

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.450
Thank you, Kenny.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.853
Thank you, 5G.

